export const pageBuilderPrompt =
  "MASTER PAGE BUILDER v3.12 \u2014 STS LANDING PAGE BUILDER\nLEAN PRODUCTION VERSION \u2014 LANDING PAGES ONLY\n\n[PROMPT_METADATA]\nversion: 3.12\ntype: landing_page_builder\npage_types: commercial landing pages only\noutput_files: 1 (html only \u2014 SEO Audit creates research brief)\nguide_pages: use Master_Guide_Builder.docx instead\n\n[V3.1_CHANGES]\nGate 6 expanded with two enforcement subsections: COMPLIANCE CLAIMS LANGUAGE (no phrasing that guarantees compliance, qualified pricing, no absolute service promises) and CERTIFICATION SCOPE (NAID AAA = data destruction only, R2v3 = recycling only, NIST 800-88 = standard not a held certification). Gate 13 Standard 12 gains two matching verification checkboxes. No instruction, pattern, or example removed. The internal metadata token PAGE_BUILDER_V3 is intentionally unchanged and remains locked for SEO Audit parsing.\n\n[V3.2_CHANGES]\nFixes the production image bug. Gate 12 IMAGE REQUIREMENTS and Gate 13 Standard 11 now require full absolute HTTPS image URLs (https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/images/2017/compressed/[file]_1920.jpg), never root-relative paths. Joomla silently fails on root-relative img src, which has been shipping broken images on every page since at least May 2026. Removed from both Bible content lists: castle-3181153 (Sugar Land confirmed broken), datacenter-286386 (Baltimore confirmed broken), data-3181149 (unverified, removed pending server confirmation), desk-4308230 (unverified, removed pending server confirmation). Confirmed-live image set retained: mac-2585220 (hero, both bibles), laptop-1742462 (content, both bibles). Gate 13 Standard 12 checklist gains one new verification line for absolute HTTPS img src. The internal metadata token PAGE_BUILDER_V3 remains unchanged.\n\n[V3.3_CHANGES]\nRestores castle-3181153, data-3181149, datacenter-286386, and desk-4308230 to the Bible content lists after server ground-truth verification (Joomla media manager listing, 2026-06-05). The v3.2 \"confirmed broken\" classification from the handoff was wrong: all four files exist live on the server. The actual bug was per-file path quirks combined with root-relative paths. Each image now has its exact verified URL hard-coded in the prompt to eliminate guessing. Two exceptions to the standard /compressed/[file]_1920.jpg pattern are documented: datacenter-286386 uses _1280 suffix (only size that exists), desk-4308230 lives at /images/2017/desk-4308230.jpg (not in /compressed/). Bible A content (3 images) and Bible B content (4 images) restored to original variety. Gate 13 Standard 11 now lists exact URLs per image. Gate 13 Standard 12 checklist updated: removed the now-incorrect \"no reference to data-3181149 or desk-4308230\" line, kept the absolute-HTTPS enforcement. The internal metadata token PAGE_BUILDER_V3 remains unchanged.\n\n[V3.4_CHANGES]\nAdds debug language to Gate 12 IMAGE REQUIREMENTS to convert image failure mode from \"silent broken image\" to \"loud halt.\" New HARD RULE forbids constructing image URLs by combining basename, suffix, and folder; the Verified image library is the complete set of allowed img src values; if a build requires an image not listed, the model must HALT with message IMAGE_NOT_VERIFIED: [basename]. This closes the class of bug that produced the v3.0 datacenter (_1920 vs _1280) and desk (/compressed/ vs root) failures by making image URL generation deterministic instead of inferential. Single-gate addition; no Gate 13 verification check added in this pass. The internal metadata token PAGE_BUILDER_V3 remains unchanged.\n\n[V3.5_CHANGES]\nTwo enforcement additions, plus matching Gate 13 verification (following the v3.1 pattern of rule-in-source-gate plus check-in-Gate-13).\n\nEm-dash guardrail. Adds EM DASHES rule to Gate 6 prohibiting em dashes (literal \u2014 character) and the &mdash; entity in generated page output (body paragraphs, headlines, FAQ answers, CTA copy, image alt text). The handoff documented em dashes appearing in every recent build (Houston 12, Jacksonville 4, NY 13) as a model generation artifact. This catches them at the source rather than relying on the Audit downstream. Gate 13 Standard 12 gains one verification line. Note: the rule applies to OUTPUT only; the prompt's own instructional prose is unaffected.\n\nEntity density target. Adds ENTITY DENSITY TARGET subsection to Gate 12 ENTITY PLACEMENT RULES. Each page should reach 12+ distinct entities total across four categories combined: named organizations (4-5 max, unchanged), regulatory entities (NIST 800-88, R2v3 standard, NAID AAA standard, niche-specific CFRs), geographic entities (CITY, COUNTY, NEIGHBORHOODS, LANDMARK from GMB), certifications and standards. Aligns with GEO-16 framework (Kumar et al, ~78% cross-engine citation rate at 12+ pillar density). Does not change the existing 4-5 named-organization cap. Gate 13 Standard 12 gains one verification line.\n\nThe internal metadata token PAGE_BUILDER_V3 remains unchanged.\n\n[V3.6_CHANGES]\nAdds a CONFLICT-PRECEDENCE LADDER to Gate 12, borrowed from the SEO Audit v10.12.2 cross-model review. Gate 12 carries competing hard requirements that can collide on short pages: word-count ceiling, the 12+ entity density target (v3.5), the 3-4 mandatory city spoke links (HALT if handoff provided and zero placed), and paragraph limits. Previously the model improvised when these could not all be satisfied, producing inconsistent behavior across the 580-page corpus. The ladder documents a fixed resolution order so the same conflict resolves the same way every time. Ordering places no-invention and preservation rules at the top (a mandatory city-spoke-link requirement must never push the model toward inventing a URL when no allowlist entry exists), mandatory city spoke links second, word ceiling third, density and link targets fourth, stylistic preferences last. Single-gate addition. No existing rule changed; this only defines precedence when existing rules conflict. The quotation soft-target check from the same handoff was evaluated and required no edit: the Builder soft-paragraph system is already generic enough to leave room for the Audit's Phase 1F Task 3 quote insertion. The internal metadata token PAGE_BUILDER_V3 remains unchanged.\n\n[V3.7_CHANGES]\nTwo additions from the cross-model judging round (2026-06-24, six-judge panel on three competing page builds). Both close defects the panel flagged on actual Page Builder output.\n\nPhone presence. The winning page in the panel shipped with no phone number at all, flagged by every judge. Gate 5 already extracts GMB PHONE and Gate 13 Standard 8 already requires tel: link formatting, but nothing guaranteed the phone actually appeared on the page. Gate 13 Standard 8 now requires the GMB PHONE to be present and visible in the contact/CTA path (hero or final CTA), not merely formatted if present. SCOPE NOTE: this Builder is GMB-mandatory (Gate 5 halts without GMB_LINK) and builds only HUB/SPOKE pages, so the phone here is always the GMB local number. The no-GMB national-page HQ toll-free rule (+1-844-699-2913) belongs to the national-page builder (Job Title Framework), not this prompt.\n\nPromotional-tone discipline. The panel (Opus 4.8 specifically) penalized shouty all-caps promotional copy (\"ABSOLUTELY FREE\") and unhedged superlatives as a 2026 E-E-A-T enforcement risk. Gate 6 gains a PROMOTIONAL TONE rule banning all-caps promotional phrases and unhedged superlatives in page output. Pairs with the existing COMPLIANCE CLAIMS LANGUAGE rule. Gate 13 Standard 12 gains one matching verification line.\n\nNo existing rule weakened. The internal metadata token PAGE_BUILDER_V3 remains unchanged.\n\n[V3.8_CHANGES]\nCorrects a sourcing error introduced in v3.5. The ENTITY DENSITY TARGET cited \"GEO-16 framework (Kumar et al): pages with 12+ pillar entities achieve ~78% cross-engine citation rate.\" Web verification (2026-07-22) against the actual paper (arXiv:2509.10762, \"AI Answer Engine Citation Behavior: An Empirical Analysis of the GEO-16 Framework,\" Arlen Kumar and Leanid Palkhouski, Sept 2025) confirmed three problems: (1) the authors are Kumar and Palkhouski, not \"Kumar et al\"; (2) the 16 pillars are page-quality signals (metadata/freshness, semantic HTML, structured data were most associated with citation), not counts of named entities; (3) the specific \"12+ entities = 78%\" statistic does not appear in the paper. That was a fabricated statistic attributed to a real source, which violates the pipeline's no-fabrication policy.\n\nFix: the rule is retained but corrected. The hard \"12+ distinct entities\" threshold becomes a soft \"roughly 10-14 distinct real entities when the content naturally supports them\" target. The false statistic and mis-citation are removed. Honest sourcing added: entity richness supports extractability, the correctly-sourced Princeton GEO research (Aggarwal et al, KDD 2024, already used by the SEO Audit) establishes statistics-with-attribution and citation as the strongest levers, and GEO-16 is described accurately as a 16-pillar page-quality audit where entity-tag density is one pillar among many, not a standalone citation rule. An explicit anti-stuffing / anti-doorway clause was added: over-stuffing named entities to hit a number is prohibited; include fewer real entities rather than manufacturing them. Changes touch the Gate 12 ENTITY DENSITY TARGET body, the Gate 12 precedence-ladder rung 4, and the Gate 13 Standard 12 entity checkbox. No other rule changed.\n\nSeparately verified but requiring no Builder change: FAQ rich results ended in Google Search on 2026-05-07 and HowTo rich results were deprecated on desktop in Sept 2023. This affects the Schema Generator, not this Builder, which emits no schema and uses FAQs as visible page content (still valuable). The v3.5 and v3.7 changelog entries above are left intact as an accurate historical record of what those versions did at the time.\n\nThe internal metadata token PAGE_BUILDER_V3 remains unchanged.\n\n[V3.9_CHANGES]\nR2/NAID location-clarity compliance patch, against R2 Compliance Patch Brief v1.2 and aligned to R2 Clean Prompt v4.8 (the production remediation prompt for the existing ~2,000 pages). A registrar review in July 2026 flagged STS city pages: an R2/NAID certification claim sitting next to a city name and a local address reads as though that local site is certified, when only Jacksonville and Houston, Texas are R2v3 certified facilities and every other STS location is a collection and service point. The Builder previously injected R2 and NAID language throughout by design, so every page it built shipped non-compliant on day one. This patch makes pages born compliant instead of remediated compliant.\n\nBecause this is a generation prompt, not an edit pass, the fix is at the source: the pattern pools, FAQ pool, hero subtitles, Gate 14 credential clustering, and entity examples are rewritten so R2/NAID never lands in a slot that cannot be made location-clear, and the mandatory sts-hq-callout is emitted natively. Additions: (1) an R2/NAID COMPLIANCE reasoning block near the top explaining the rule, the two-jobs framing, and both failure modes; (2) a Gate 6 R2/NAID LOCATION CLARITY rule carrying the budget, approved vocabulary, rotation, the two exemptions (educational, negative-scope disclaimer), and the mandatory callout; (3) Gate 12 emits the sts-hq-callout block (converting the compliance/certifications card where possible); (4) rewritten COMPLIANCE/SERVICE/ENTITY/HERO pattern pools and the certifications FAQ; (5) Gate 14 credential clustering made location-clear; (6) Gate 13 Standard 12 R2/NAID compliance verification checks. Scope is R2 and NAID only, visible page text only; head/meta/og/alt/schema are out of scope and untouched (Josh ruled \"text on page\"). Every other certification (NIST, HIPAA, ISO 27001, DoD, SOC 2, FISMA, FERPA, SOX, GLBA, FACTA, EPA, RIOS, e-Stewards) is left exactly as before. Budget is 3 or fewer in-scope mentions in visible text page-wide, all location-clear; NAID gets zero survivors until facility scope is confirmed. The internal metadata token PAGE_BUILDER_V3 remains unchanged.\n\n[V3.10_CHANGES]\nApplies the four v2.1 deltas from R2 Compliance Patch Brief Universal v2.1 (Josh Crow rulings, August 2 2026), aligned to R2 Clean Prompt v4.9. This prompt is Category A (city-targeted with a local address), so full treatment is retained: budget of 3, location clarity, mandatory callout. Two deltas LOOSEN prior restrictions.\n\nDELTA 1, loosening. Only the literal string \"R2v3\" triggers the location-clarity rule. Plain \"certified\" does not, and is reopened for H1s, section headings, and body prose where it carries keyword value (\"Certified Electronics Recycling for {CITY}\" is allowed with no Jacksonville/Houston). It stays banned in short slots (trust chips, badge labels, card titles, stat labels) where a bare \"Certified\" beside \"NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2\" looks broken. Flagged in-prompt as Josh's read of Clasen, which conflicts with Clasen's earlier direct wording; if Clasen contradicts it later, remove \"certified\" from the vocabulary and nothing else changes.\n\nDELTA 2, loosening. Square footage is not a certification claim: it does not count against the budget, needs no location qualifier, is never stripped, and is never city-qualified. Where a size figure shares a sentence with an R2/NAID claim, the claim is fixed and the number kept. The number itself is DISPUTED (prompts and pages say 600,000; the COO and Mark said 200,000 on the call) and is deliberately left unchanged everywhere pending a COO ruling. All nine occurrences in this file are reported in the delivery notes and untouched.\n\nDELTA 3. Meta tags are out of scope for the budget AND should actively carry R2v3 for click-through. The Gate 10 meta description template now uses the COO-approved shape \"R2v3 certified electronics recycling for {CITY} businesses.\" Noted in-prompt that on standalone pages the in-file head does not render and Joomla article fields govern live meta, so the highest-value meta work is a CMS task.\n\nDELTA 4. NAID remains at ZERO SURVIVORS, restructured as a one-line flip (NAID_SURVIVORS_ENABLED = NO). The reported Houston-only scope is recorded as FLAGGED and explicitly not acted on, because it came from a garbled auto-transcript and is a factual certification-scope claim. When confirmed in writing, flip to YES and NAID becomes eligible for slot 3 naming Houston only, never Jacksonville; budget stays at 3.\n\nPENDING. A dedicated R2v3 authority page was proposed for city pages to link to. It does not exist yet, so Gate 12 internal linking now carries an explicitly empty reserved slot (Step 4) with a hard instruction not to invent or construct its URL.\n\nThe internal metadata token PAGE_BUILDER_V3 remains unchanged.\n\n[V3.11_CHANGES]\nAttribution layer completion. The Builder carried 2 of the canonical attribution layers (HTML comment, meta author); the canonical creator-attribution system is 3 invisible layers plus the Schema Generator's JSON-LD Person entity. Adds Layer 3, the hidden CREATOR_ENTITY comment block, immediately before </body>. Rewrote the surrounding ATTRIBUTION rules, which previously said \"No URLs. Head section only\" and would have contradicted Layer 3 (it carries the LinkedIn URL and sits at end of body). Rules now read: no visible text, no footer credit, Layers 1-2 head-only, Layer 3 an HTML comment at end of body, URLs only inside that comment.\nDELIBERATELY NOT ADDED: the aria-hidden clipped attribution div (the fourth layer used by some other prompts in the family). It renders text that is hidden from users, which is a cloaking risk under Google's current spam policy. Shipping it across 580+ pages during an active certification review is not a justified trade. If it is wanted later it is a one-block addition, but it should be an explicit decision.\nNo other rule changed. Square footage figures untouched. NAID_SURVIVORS_ENABLED remains NO. The internal metadata token PAGE_BUILDER_V3 remains unchanged.\n\n[V3.12_CHANGES]\nSQUARE FOOTAGE RESOLVED: 600,000 corrected to 200,000 throughout, on operator authorization (August 2026). This reverses the v3.10 \"FLAGGED, DO NOT ACT ON\" hold. Seven operational occurrences changed: the Gate 6 facility-size-plus-location examples (2), the Gate 6 approved-patterns example, the FACILITY SIZE rule, the square-footage rule example, SERVICE PATTERN A, and HERO SUBTITLE PATTERN D. The FACILITY SIZE correction list now includes 600,000 and 600K as values to correct TO 200,000, so the Builder fixes legacy pages carrying the old figure. Four references to 600,000 remain deliberately: one historical changelog line, one inside that correction list, and two resolution notes. Zero remain in any output pattern.\nBASIS AND REVERSIBILITY: this change was made on operator authorization, not on independent verification. The figure was recorded as disputed in v3.10 (prompts and pages said 600,000; the COO and Mark said 200,000 on the August 2 call). Other STS prompts and roughly 2,000 live pages may still carry 600,000 and will need the same correction. If 200,000 later proves wrong, reverting is a search-and-replace of the same seven locations.\nNAID DELIBERATELY NOT FLIPPED: NAID_SURVIVORS_ENABLED remains NO. The authorization covered R2 and square footage; NAID facility scope is a separate factual claim still resting on a garbled auto-transcript and still requires written confirmation. Flipping it would place a certification claim on every page built from here forward based on unverified transcription. When confirmed in writing, set the flag to YES; NAID then names Houston only, never Jacksonville.\nR2 STATE VERIFIED THIS PASS: all pattern pools free of bare R2/NAID claims; sts-hq-callout mandatory and present; NAID zero survivors; dedicated R2v3 authority page link slot reserved and empty with no invented URL; meta template carries R2v3 per Delta 3; \"certified\" permitted in long slots and banned in short slots per Delta 1.\nThe internal metadata token PAGE_BUILDER_V3 remains unchanged.\n\n[EXECUTION_MODE]\nmode: SILENT_EXECUTION\nAll gates execute silently. Suppress progress updates, gate confirmations, self-checks, optimization details, technical validations, and metadata display. Show only critical errors that block progress and final deliverables with download links. Final delivery format: \"\u2705 {CITY} complete. File ready.\" + download link.\n\n[R2_NAID_COMPLIANCE_WHY]\nRead this before generating any R2 or NAID language. It decides the close calls.\n\nA registrar review flagged STS city pages: a certification claim sitting beside a city name and a local address reads as though the local site is certified. Only two STS sites are R2v3 certified facilities, Jacksonville and Houston, Texas. Every other STS location is a collection and service point. STS IS R2v3 certified and is still allowed to say so; what is not allowed is leaving it ambiguous where the certification lives.\n\nTHE RULE. On any page that targets a city and carries a local address, a certification claim is only acceptable if the sentence making the claim also names Jacksonville or Houston in that same sentence. Not the paragraph, not a nearby block, the same sentence.\n\nTWO JOBS, AND DOING ONLY THE FIRST IS A FAILURE.\nOne: stop implying local certification.\nTwo: keep the page reading like what STS actually is, a credentialed operator running since 2011 across all 50 states. A page that comes out reading as though STS holds no certifications has FAILED, even if it contains zero instances of R2.\n\nBoth failure directions are real and both already happened on this project:\n- A certifications FAQ answered with no certification in it. Empty answer reads as uncertified; worse than the original problem.\n- A fabricated \"Per EPA 40 CFR 261\" citation swapped in to replace R2. A plausible but wrong citation on a compliance page during a certification review is the worst possible output.\n\nThe approach is volume plus clarity: cut in-scope mentions way down, make the few survivors fully location-clear, and give everything else approved wording that carries the same meaning without naming the scheme. The full allocation, vocabulary, exemptions, and the mandatory callout are in the Gate 6 R2/NAID LOCATION CLARITY rule. Never invent or substitute a different standard to fill a gap: drop the citation and state the fact plainly, or make it location-clear.\n\n[REQUIRED_INPUTS]\nMaster Design Bible CODE (.docx) \u2014 HTML structure and CSS template\nSTS SEO DATA 2026 (.xlsx) \u2014 Page performance metrics\nHandoff Document (.md) \u2014 OPTIONAL \u2014 City sibling page URLs + local context\nUser provides: page_url, gmb_url, gmb_data (screenshot or text)\n\n[GLOBAL_VARIABLES]\nFROM_URL: CITY, STATE (2-letter), SERVICE\nFROM_GMB: GMB_LINK, ADDRESS, PHONE (XXX-XXX-XXXX), CID, CID_DECIMAL, CID_NORMALIZED, ZIP, COUNTY, NEIGHBORHOODS, LANDMARK, LAT, LNG, OPEN_TIME, CLOSE_TIME\nFROM_RESEARCH: COMPETITION_LEVEL (LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH), FINAL_TARGET, COMPETITOR_AVG_WORDCOUNT, KEYWORDS_LONGTAIL (5), KEYWORDS_POPULAR (5)\nFROM_CLASSIFICATION: PAGE_CLASSIFICATION (LIGHT_TOUCH|REVAMP|NEW_BUILD), CONTENT_PRESERVATION_PERCENTAGE, CURRENT_CLICKS, CURRENT_POSITION\nFROM_STRATEGY: PAGE_TYPE (HUB|SPOKE), META_TITLE, META_DESCRIPTION, META_KEYWORDS (8), SELECTED_BENEFITS (6)\nFROM_CITY_RESEARCH: CITY_UNIQUE_SENTENCES (2-3), CITY_INDUSTRY_CONTEXT, CITY_GEOGRAPHIC_FACTS\nFROM_HANDOFF: RELATED_PAGES (3-6 URLs), HANDOFF_ENTITIES, TIER_STRUCTURE\n\n[GATE_1_PAGE_TYPE_DETECTION]\npriority: CRITICAL \u2014 execute first before any processing\nExtract URL from user input. Check for guide keyword. IF \"guide\" in URL.lowercase(): HALT: \"\u26d4 WRONG PROMPT. This URL is a guide page. Use Master_Guide_Builder.docx. Do not proceed.\" EXIT. ELSE: proceed to Gate 2.\n\n[GATE_2_PREFLIGHT]\nExtract from URL: CITY, STATE, SERVICE. Validate all non-empty, STATE length==2. Validate files: Master Design Bible CODE uploaded, STS SEO DATA Excel uploaded, Handoff document (check if present). GMB CID conversion: Extract hex CID from GMB URL. Convert hex to decimal. Store as CID_DECIMAL and CID_NORMALIZED (format: \"cid:XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\"). Design Bible selection: If user specifies bible, use that. Otherwise Hash(CITY+STATE) mod 2 \u2192 0=Bible A, 1=Bible B. Store as BIBLE_VERSION. On fail: halt with error.\n\n[GATE_3_HUB_SPOKE]\nIF url contains \"{city}-electronics-recycling\" OR \"{city}-e-waste\": PAGE_TYPE = HUB, COMMERCIAL_OPTIMIZATION = false\nELSE: PAGE_TYPE = SPOKE, COMMERCIAL_OPTIMIZATION = true\n\n[GATE_4_HANDOFF_LOADER]\nConditional \u2014 only if handoff file provided. IF handoff found: Parse markdown. Extract: city_context, state_context, total_pages, all page URLs with tier assignments. Identify current page tier by matching URL. Build RELATED_PAGES array (3-6 URLs): priority Tier 1 \u2192 related services \u2192 same tier. Build TIER_STRUCTURE: store tier assignment for each URL for link priority in Gate 12. Extract Local Context section as HANDOFF_ENTITIES array: entity names, specific data points (bed counts, revenue, student counts, employee counts). These are pre-curated \u2014 skip verification, available for Gate 11 and Gate 12. ELSE: RELATED_PAGES = empty, HANDOFF_ENTITIES = empty, use corporate links only.\n\n[GATE_5_GMB_COLLECTION]\nGMB_LINK is mandatory. If missing: request from user and halt. Extract: ADDRESS, PHONE, CID (convert to decimal), ZIP, COUNTY, NEIGHBORHOODS, LANDMARK, LAT, LNG, OPEN_TIME (default 08:00), CLOSE_TIME (default 17:00). Validate: GMB_LINK pattern (maps.app.goo.gl or google.com/maps), CID numeric 15-20 digits, PHONE format XXX-XXX-XXXX, LAT range [-90,90], LNG range [-180,180]. On fail: halt.\n\n[GATE_6_FACILITY_LANGUAGE]\nStore these rules for enforcement in Gate 12 and Gate 13.\n\nFORBIDDEN PATTERNS \u2014 never use in any output: \"facility in {CITY}\", \"our {CITY} facility\", \"{CITY} facility\", \"{CITY} location\", \"{CITY} recycling center\", \"{CITY} warehouse\", \"located in {CITY}\", \"our {CITY} office\", \"sales office in {CITY}\", \"recycling facility in {CITY}\", \"visit our facility in {CITY}\", \"the {CITY} facility\"\n\nFacility size" +
  " + location: \"Our 200,000 sq ft facility in {CITY}\" \u2014 FORBIDDEN. \"Our 200,000 sq ft facility serves {CITY}\" \u2014 APPROVED.\n\nAPPROVED PATTERNS: \"We serve {CITY} from our 200,000 sq ft processing operation\" \"Our secure fleet serves {CITY} with scheduled pickups\" \"{CITY} electronics recycling services\" / \"secure processing for {CITY}\"\nNOTE: the former \"R2v3 certified facility\" and \"R2 certified processing for {CITY}\" example patterns were removed in v3.9. A certification claim next to {CITY} and a local address is exactly the location-ambiguity the registrar flagged. See the Gate 6 R2/NAID LOCATION CLARITY rule; certification claims live only in the location-clear survivor slots.\n\nFACILITY SIZE: Always 200,000 sq ft. If input HTML contains ANY facility size other than 200,000 (including 600,000, 600K, 50,000, 50K, 150,000, 150K, or any other value), correct ALL instances to 200,000 sq ft. RESOLVED v3.12: the prior 600,000 figure was corrected to 200,000 on operator authorization (August 2026). Legacy pages and other prompts may still carry 600,000; treat 200,000 as canonical here.\n\nNEGATIVE SCOPE \u2014 STS doesn't offer: \"paper shredding\", \"document shredding\", \"file destruction\", \"records shredding\" \u2192 Replace with \"hard drive destruction\" or \"digital media destruction\"\n\nEM DASHES. Never use em dashes (the literal \u2014 character) or the &mdash; HTML entity in generated page output. This applies to all body paragraphs, headlines, FAQ answers, CTA copy, and image alt text. Use commas, semicolons, periods, or parentheses for the same separation function. The SEO Audit catches em dashes downstream, but they are a model generation artifact that must be prevented at the source. This rule applies to page OUTPUT only; the prompt's own instructional prose is unaffected.\n\nPROMOTIONAL TONE. Keep page copy factual and restrained. Forbidden in output: all-caps promotional phrases (\"ABSOLUTELY FREE\", \"100% FREE\", \"BEST IN CLASS\"), exclamation-driven promo, and unhedged superlatives (\"the best\", \"the only\", \"guaranteed lowest\", \"unbeatable\"). Shouty promotional tone is a 2026 E-E-A-T and AI-citation risk: answer engines and Google's current enforcement reward plain, hedged, factual phrasing over sales language. Approved: \"free pickup for qualifying volumes\", \"trusted by\", \"certified\", factual benefit statements. This is distinct from the COMPLIANCE CLAIMS LANGUAGE rule above (which governs regulatory claims); this rule governs promotional register. Applies to page OUTPUT only.\n\nCOMPLIANCE CLAIMS LANGUAGE. STS content describes compliance support, never guaranteed regulatory outcomes. This applies to every niche, with highest priority on healthcare, financial, and government pages where compliance content is densest.\nFORBIDDEN: \"guarantees compliance\", \"guarantees HIPAA compliance\", \"ensures compliance\", \"meets all {regulation} requirements\", \"fully compliant\", \"100% compliant\", or any phrasing that promises a regulatory outcome.\nAPPROVED: \"helps meet {regulation} requirements\", \"supports {regulation} compliance\", \"designed to support compliance with {regulation}\", \"documentation that supports {regulation} audits\".\nABSOLUTE PROMISES: replace \"always\", \"guaranteed\", and \"same-day guaranteed\" with \"typically\", \"generally\", or \"most organizations\". Existing timeline specifics from Gate 14 (e.g. \"same-week pickup\", \"Certificate within 48 hours\") are factual service descriptions and remain approved.\nPRICING: \"free pickup\" is permitted because pickup is genuinely free. Any broader free-service claim must be qualified, e.g. \"free recycling for qualifying volumes\". Never state specific prices.\n\nCERTIFICATION SCOPE. State each certification only in its correct scope. Conflated certification claims are factually wrong and undermine the authority the page is built to project.\nNAID AAA: data destruction only. Correct usage: \"NAID AAA certified data destruction\", \"NAID AAA certified hard drive shredding\". Forbidden: \"NAID AAA certified recycling\", \"NAID certified electronics recycling\".\nR2v3: electronics recycling and responsible downstream processing only. Correct SCOPE usage (recycling context, not data destruction): \"R2v3 certified processing\", \"R2v3 certified electronics recycling\". Forbidden scope error: \"R2 certified data destruction\", \"R2v3 certified shredding\". NOTE: scope-correct is not the same as location-clear. Any R2v3 claim in visible page text must also satisfy the R2/NAID LOCATION CLARITY rule below, which is why bare \"R2v3 certified facility\" next to a city is not usable in output; it appears only in a location-clear survivor naming Jacksonville or Houston.\nNIST 800-88: a data sanitization standard, not a certification STS holds. Correct usage: \"destruction that exceeds NIST 800-88\", \"NIST 800-88 compliant destruction\". Forbidden: \"NIST 800-88 certified\".\nWhen one sentence spans both destruction and recycling, name both certifications in their correct scope. Do not blend them into a single claim.\n\nR2/NAID LOCATION CLARITY. Enforces the registrar location-clarity finding (see [R2_NAID_COMPLIANCE_WHY]). Scope: R2 and NAID only, in visible page text only. In-scope strings: R2, R2v3, R2:2020, Responsible Recycling, NAID, NAID AAA. Out of scope and untouched: title/meta/og/alt/schema/HTML comments, and every other standard (NIST, HIPAA, ISO 27001, DoD 5220.22-M, SOC 2, FISMA, FERPA, SOX, GLBA, FACTA, EPA, RIOS, e-Stewards).\n\nBUDGET: 3 or fewer in-scope mentions in visible page text, page-wide, counting R2 and NAID strings together (not 3 each). Educational mentions, the negative-scope disclaimer, and head/meta/og/alt/schema do NOT count against the budget.\n\nWHERE THE THREE GO, in this order:\nSlot 1 MANDATORY: the sts-hq-callout block (see Gate 12). Every page carries it. This is the survivor that satisfies the consultant.\nSlot 2 STRONGLY PREFERRED: the front-loaded answer block, if generated. Keep the certification and make it location-clear in the same sentence. WATCH WORD COUNT: the block must stay 40-60 words. Working 42-word shape: \"STS Electronic Recycling provides R2v3 certified electronics recycling for {CITY} businesses, processed at our Jacksonville, Texas and Houston, Texas facilities. Operating since 2011, STS handles scheduled pickup, serial-number certificates of destruction, and downstream material tracking through final processing for {COUNTY} County organizations.\"\nSlot 3 OPTIONAL: the certifications FAQ answer, if generated, made location-clear (see FAQ pool). An answer naming no certification is a FAILURE.\n\nWHERE THE THREE NEVER GO (these always get an approved replacement, never a survivor): trust bar chips, badge labels, stat band values and labels, card titles, H1 and section headings, hero subtitles, link anchor text, final CTA, any template too short to name a city. A short slot cannot be made location-clear, so replacement is the only correct answer.\n\nEVERY SURVIVOR NAMES A CITY IN ITS OWN SENTENCE. The same sentence that makes the claim names Jacksonville or Houston. A survivor that is not location-clear is a FAILURE, not a partial win.\n\nNAID_SURVIVORS_ENABLED = NO   <-- THE ONE-LINE FLIP. Change to YES only when facility scope is confirmed in writing.\nNAID: ZERO SURVIVORS while NAID_SURVIVORS_ENABLED = NO. Every NAID/NAID AAA mention in visible text gets an approved replacement. Reason is mechanical: a survivor must name its certified location in its own sentence, and we cannot write a true location-clear NAID sentence without knowing its scope.\nFLAGGED, DO NOT ACT ON: NAID is reported as Houston only, not Jacksonville (\"NAID, you do say Houston. You can't say Jacksonville.\"). That line came off a garbled auto-transcript and is a factual claim about certification scope. Acting on it would put a certification claim on 2,000 pages based on a transcription. It is NOT confirmed and must not be used.\nWHEN CONFIRMED IN WRITING: set NAID_SURVIVORS_ENABLED = YES. NAID then becomes eligible for slot 3 naming HOUSTON ONLY, never Jacksonville. Budget stays at 3. Nothing else changes.\n\nAPPROVED VOCABULARY (Josh Crow approved exactly these; do not invent alternatives or reach for a better-seeming synonym): Secure Recycling, Accurate Reporting, Chain of Custody, Secure, Transparent, Sustainable. The three single-word modifiers can stand alone, pair, or run as a triad by slot. What each carries: Secure Recycling = data security + service noun (strong search value); Accurate Reporting = documentation/audit-trail half; Chain of Custody = tracked handling pickup through final processing; Secure = data protection; Transparent = documented/auditable; Sustainable = environmental half.\nNEVER use \"Responsible Recycling\", \"Responsible Processing\", or \"Responsibly Recycled\" as a replacement (that restates the R2 trademark in longhand).\nTRIGGER STRING: only the literal string \"R2v3\" (and the other in-scope strings above) triggers the location-clarity rule. Plain \"certified\" does NOT trigger it. Josh Crow, relaying Clasen: \"If it says R2v3, that's where it needs to be clear. So if you say audited by third parties, then that's not saying the words R2v3. So that feels pretty okay.\"\nThe word \"certified\" IS ALLOWED in H1s, section headings, and body prose, where it carries real keyword value. \"Certified Electronics Recycling for {CITY}\" is allowed and needs no Jacksonville/Houston, because it does not contain R2v3.\nThe word \"certified\" is NOT allowed in short slots: trust bar chips, badge labels, card titles, and stat labels. The approved short-slot terms already work there, and a bare \"Certified\" beside \"NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2\" looks broken. That happened in production. Never pair \"certified\" with a location-implying noun in a short slot.\nFLAGGED: this is Josh's read of Clasen, not Clasen's direct words. The earlier Clasen quote was \"any time you advertise that you are certified.\" Those conflict. Follow Josh. If Clasen contradicts it later, remove \"certified\" from the approved vocabulary and nothing else changes.\n\nSQUARE FOOTAGE IS NOT A CERTIFICATION CLAIM. A facility size figure does not count against the budget and needs no Jacksonville or Houston in its sentence. Do not strip it and do not add a city to it. Where a size figure sits in the same sentence as an R2 or NAID claim, fix the claim and keep the number: \"from our 200,000 sq ft R2v3 certified facility\" becomes \"from our 200,000 sq ft processing operation\", keeping the figure.\nRESOLVED (was FLAGGED in v3.10): the square footage figure is 200,000 sq ft. The prior 600,000 figure was incorrect and was corrected throughout this prompt in v3.12 on operator authorization. Use 200,000 in all output. If any input HTML or legacy page carries 600,000, correct it to 200,000.\nNO LOCATION-IMPLYING NOUNS in a replacement (facility, center, plant, site, location, warehouse) unless that same element names Jacksonville or Houston.\nNEVER swap in a different standard. If a template cites R2v3 or NAID, either drop the citation and state the fact plainly, or make it location-clear. Do not substitute another authority or invent a CFR/ISO number.\n\nBY-SLOT REPLACEMENT:\nH1/section headings: lead with Secure. \"R2 Certified Electronics Recycling for {CITY}\" to \"Secure Electronics Recycling for {CITY}\".\nBody inline: \"R2v3 certified electronics recycling\" to \"secure electronics recycling\"; \"our R2 certified facility\" to \"our secure processing facility\"; \"NAID AAA certified data destruction\" to \"secure data destruction\".\nParagraph/long-form (triad works): \"R2v3 certified processing\" to \"secure, transparent, sustainable processing\"; \"R2v3 certification ensures downstream tracking\" to \"chain of custody documentation tracks every asset through final processing\".\nCard titles (2-4 words, match sibling specificity): \"R2v3 Certified Processing\" to \"Chain of Custody\"; \"NAID AAA Certified\" to \"Secure Data Destruction\".\nTrust chips/badges (2-3 words, keep grid child count): \"R2v3 Certified\" to \"Secure Recycling\"; \"NAID AAA\" to \"Accurate Reporting\".\nStat tokens (value under 5 chars, replace value AND label together, never orphan one): value \"R2\" + label \"CERTIFIED RECYCLING\" to value \"100%\" + label \"SECURE PROCESSING\", or value \"TWO\" + label \"TEXAS PROCESSING FACILITIES\".\nLink anchor text: keep destination page's own term first; \"R2v3 certified electronics recycling\" to \"secure electronics recycling\".\n\nROTATION: never use the same replacement twice in one section; use at least three different approved terms across the page; never the same term in two adjacent elements; pick on meaning first, rotation is the tiebreaker. Across 580+ pages, do not let one replacement word appear everywhere.\n\nTWO EXEMPTIONS, never counted and never failed:\nEDUCATIONAL mentions. A sentence teaching what a standard requires or what a buyer should look for, making no claim about STS. THE TEST: remove STS from the sentence; if it is still true and sensible, it is education. Example: \"When evaluating {SERVICE} providers, {PERSONA}s at organizations like {ENTITY} prioritize R2v3 certification and downstream documentation.\" Preserve these; never convert one into the callout; deleting a standard from a neutral checklist makes guidance worse, not safer.\nNEGATIVE-SCOPE DISCLAIMER. A sentence that denies certification at the local city. It contains R2v3, names the local city, and names neither Jacksonville nor Houston, because its job is to deny local certification. THE TEST: does the sentence ASSERT certification here, or DENY it? Assert is in scope; deny is exempt. Example: \"Our {CITY} location is a collection and service point. It is not an R2v3 certified processing facility.\" Optional, defaults OFF, emitted only if SCOPE_LINE = YES.\n\n[GATE_7_CURRENT_PAGE_ANALYSIS]\ntool: web_fetch on PAGE_URL\nIF page not found: CURRENT_WORDCOUNT = 0, EXISTING_CONTENT = none, mark NEW_BUILD.\nELSE: extract CURRENT_WORDCOUNT, EXISTING_CONTENT, UNIQUE_CITY_CONTENT.\n\n[GATE_8_COMPETITOR_RESEARCH_AND_DEPTH]\ntool: web_search for \"{SERVICE} {CITY} {STATE}\" Identify top 3-5 commercial competitors (exclude government sites).\nFor each competitor, estimate: word_count, service_depth (basic|comprehensive), content_quality (low|medium|high).\nCalculate COMPETITOR_AVG = sum(word_counts) / count(competitors). If zero competitors found: COMPETITION_LEVEL = LOW, COMPETITOR_AVG = 400, FINAL_TARGET = DESIGN_BIBLE_FLOOR (2,000).\nAssess quality and set multiplier: WEAK (avg < 500): 1.5x-2x DECENT (avg 500-1200): 2x-2.5x STRONG (avg > 1200): 2.5x-3x\nCalculate: BASE_TARGET = COMPETITOR_AVG \u00d7 MULTIPLIER\nApply DESIGN_BIBLE_FLOOR and ceilings: DESIGN_BIBLE_FLOOR = 2,000 (minimum viable output with trimmed bibles) LOW ceiling = 2,400 MEDIUM ceiling = 2,800 HIGH ceiling = 3,200 FINAL_TARGET = MAX(MIN(BASE_TARGET, CEILING), DESIGN_BIBLE_FLOOR)\nValidate: FINAL_TARGET >= 1.5x COMPETITOR_AVG, FINAL_TARGET <= 3x COMPETITOR_AVG.\nClassify competition: LOW: few competitors, weak content, government-only results MEDIUM: 2-3 strong competitors, decent depth HIGH: multiple strong competitors, comprehensive content\nExtract keywords: 5 longtail (city+service specific), 5 popular (broader industry).\nStore: COMPETITION_LEVEL, FINAL_TARGET, COMPETITOR_AVG_WORDCOUNT, KEYWORDS_LONGTAIL, KEYWORDS_POPULAR.\n\n[GATE_9_PAGE_CLASSIFICATION]\nSource: STS_SEO_DATA_2026.xlsx (Pages tab). Lookup PAGE_URL. Extract: CLICKS, IMPRESSIONS, POSITION, CTR.\nLIGHT_TOUCH: clicks > 500 OR position \u2264 10 OR impressions > 50000 \u2192 preservation 70% REVAMP: clicks 100-500 OR position 11-30 \u2192 preservation 50% NEW_BUILD: clicks < 100 OR position > 30 OR page missing \u2192 preservation 0%\nStore: PAGE_CLASSIFICATION, CONTENT_PRESERVATION_PERCENTAGE, CURRENT_CLICKS, CURRENT_POSITION.\n\n[GATE_10_META_STRATEGY_AND_ROLE_BENEFITS]\nGenerate meta tags: Title: \"{SERVICE} {CITY} {STATE} | {USP} | STS Recycling\" \u2014 60-80 chars Description: use the COO-approved shape carrying R2v3: \"R2v3 certified electronics recycling for {CITY} businesses. {benefits}. Call {PHONE}.\" \u2014 150-160 chars. Keywords: best 8 from KEYWORDS_LONGTAIL + KEYWORDS_POPULAR Store META_TITLE, META_DESCRIPTION, META_KEYWORDS for HTML head. Not displayed during execution.\nMETA IS OUT OF SCOPE FOR THE R2 BUDGET AND SHOULD CARRY R2v3. This is a preference, not just permission. Josh Crow wants R2v3 in the meta description for click-through. His reasoning: \"we're not saying the facility's in Chicago, we're saying we're servicing the Chicago area, which is totally true.\" Meta/title/og/alt/schema never count against the 3-mention budget and never need a Jacksonville/Houston qualifier. NOTE: on standalone pages the in-file head does not render; Joomla article fields govern the live title and description, so the highest-value meta work is a CMS task, not a prompt task.\nDetermine PRIMARY_ROLE from SERVICE: data_destruction \u2192 Compliance Officer (benefits: Certificate of Destruction, NAID AAA) hard_drive_shredding \u2192 IT Security Manager (benefits: Data Security, NAID AAA) itad \u2192 Procurement Manager (benefits: Asset Remarketing, Free Pickup) asset_lifecycle \u2192 Facilities Manager (benefits: Free Pickup, Logistics Support)\nSelect 6 benefits: 2 industry-matched, 2 role-matched, 2 variety. Store SELECTED_BENEFITS.\n\n[GATE_11_CITY_RESEARCH]\nPurpose: Generate genuinely unique local content no template can produce.\nStep 1: Check HANDOFF_ENTITIES from Gate 4. If populated, use as primary entity source. Step 2: Web search \"{CITY} {STATE} major industries business landscape\" (one search call). Step 3: From results + handoff data, extract: CITY_UNIQUE_SENTENCES: 2-3 sentences about the city's specific business landscape, industry trends, or geographic significance \u2014 facts unique to this city, not generic statements. Example: \"Chicago's financial exchange corridor (CME Group, CBOE) creates concentrated compliance pressure for certified data destruction.\" CITY_INDUSTRY_CONTEXT: Dominant sector discovered. Validates or overrides niche from URL slug. CITY_GEOGRAPHIC_FACTS: Corridors, districts, regional identity beyond GMB data. Step 4: If handoff provided, supplement \u2014 don't duplicate handoff data.\nFailure handling: If search returns no useful city-specific data, set CITY_UNIQUE_SENTENCES = empty. Gate 12 uses sentence pattern pools as fallback. Log: \"Gate 11: no unique city content found.\"\n\n[GATE_12_HTML_BUILD]\nCONFLICT-PRECEDENCE LADDER. When the rules in this gate cannot all be satisfied at once (common on LOW-competition short pages where word ceiling, entity density, mandatory links, and paragraph limits compete), resolve in this fixed order. Do not improvise.\n1. NO-INVENTION AND PRESERVATION: Never invent URLs, entities, facts, employee counts, or image paths. Never violate facility language, compliance claims, or certification scope rules from Gate 6. These never yield to any other rule.\n2. MANDATORY CITY SPOKE LINKS: If a handoff was provided, 3-4 city spoke links are required (HALT condition). Yields only to rung 1. If satisfying the link count would require inventing a URL, rung 1 wins and the model places only the links that exist in the handoff or allowlist, then proceeds.\n3. WORD-COUNT CEILING: The hard ceiling (LOW 2,400 / MED 2,800 / HIGH 3,200) is enforced over density and link-density targets. Yields only to rungs 1 and 2. Trim Optional then Preferred sections to stay under ceiling.\n4. ENTITY DENSITY AND LINK TARGETS: The entity-richness target (roughly 10-14 distinct real entities) and link distribution preferences yield to rungs 1-3. Hit them as fully as the ceiling allows; never breach the ceiling or manufacture entities to reach a number.\n5. STYLISTIC AND DISTRIBUTION PREFERENCES: Paragraph spacing, entity spacing (3+ paragraphs apart), pattern rotation. Lowest priority; yield to all above.\nWhen a conflict is resolved by this ladder, note it in the build log: \"Conflict resolved: [lower rule] yielded to [higher rule] per precedence ladder.\"\n\nCRITICAL: MASTER DESIGN BIBLE EXACT USAGE Before any HTML generation:\nExtract FULL Master Design Bible CODE using python-docx or equivalent\nRead ENTIRE document structure start to finish\nStore complete HTML structure in memory \u2014 this is the EXACT code template\nVerify: complete HTML from <!DOCTYPE> to </html> IF extraction incomplete: HARD STOP \u2014 request verification of upload.\nMASTER CODE RULES \u2014 NEVER MODIFY: CSS (colors, fonts, spacing, animations), layouts (grid-2/3/4), card styling, button styles, mobile breakpoints, hero structure, form placement, location section, HTML structure (divs, sections, classes), any <style> blocks.\nMODIFY ONLY: Variable placeholders ({CITY}, {STATE}, {SERVICE}, {PHONE}, etc.), paragraph text content, headlines (H1/H2/H3), image alt tags, anchor text in links, WHICH SECTIONS TO INCLUDE (per section priority below).\n\nSECTION PRIORITY SYSTEM Controls which Design Bible sections appear based on competition level.\nREQUIRED (always include): Hero (with form), Equipment showcase (sacred links), Final CTA + Map\nPREFERRED (include for MEDIUM and HIGH): Industries/verticals, FAQ, Compliance/NIST block, Service areas + About City\nOPTIONAL (include for HIGH only): Stats bar, Specialized services, Liquidation CTA, \"Why Choose STS\" cards\nLOW competition = Required + 2 best Preferred sections for this niche (~2,000-2,400 words) MEDIUM competition = Required + all Preferred (~2,400-2,800 words) HIGH competition = Required + all Preferred + 2-3 Optional (~2,800-3,200 words)\nBelow DESIGN_BIBLE_FLOOR: exclude optional sections per this priority. Never compress all sections into fewer words.\n\nNICHE CONTENT MATRIX Controls WHICH content blocks appear based on detected niche. Primary uniqueness lever for same-city pages.\nHEALTHCARE: Include PHI workflow, BAA block, clinical refresh. Exclude enterprise ITAD, asset recovery ROI. Industries \u2192 hospitals, clinics, health systems. Compliance \u2192 HIPAA 45 CFR \u00a7164.312, BAAs, PHI chain-of-custody.\nCORPORATE/ITAD: Include asset recovery ROI, depreciation, lease return. Exclude PHI, clinical. Industries \u2192 Fortune 500, enterprise, multi-site. Compliance \u2192 SOC 2, ISO 27001, asset tagging.\nDATA DESTRUCTION: Include chain-of-custody detail, witnessed destruction, NSA/CSS EPL specs. Exclude asset recovery, liquidation. Compliance block expanded \u2192 NIST 800-88 Rev. 1, DoD 5220.22-M, NAID AAA.\nGOVERNMENT: Include procurement compliance, multi-building coordination, OMB/FISMA. Exclude asset recovery, liquidation. Industries \u2192 state, county, federal, municipal. Compliance \u2192 FISMA, OMB A-123.\nEDUCATION: Include academic calendar scheduling, FERPA, district purchasing. Exclude data center decom, enterprise-scale. Industries \u2192 K-12, university, district. Compliance \u2192 FERPA, budget cycles.\nFINANCIAL: Include SOX/GLBA block, witnessed destruction for financial records. Exclude PHI, academic. Industries \u2192 banks, exchanges, insurance. Compliance \u2192 SOX 404, GLBA 16 CFR Part 314.\nGENERAL/HUB: Broad industry coverage, all equipment, geographic depth. No single-industry focus. Compliance \u2192 overview-level R2v3, NIST, HIPAA.\n\nSENTENCE PATTERN POOLS 7 categories, 29 patterns. Rotate per city. Selection: Hash(CITY) mod N = starting pattern. Advance sequentially for multiple uses on same page \u2014 never repeat a pattern on one page.\nENTITY PATTERNS (use 1-2 per page; these are STS claims, so keep them R2/NAID-free per the location-clarity rule. For the exempt educational buyer-criteria shape, see the note below): A: \"Organizations like {ENTITY} and {ENTITY_2} rely on STS for {SERVICE}\" B: \"STS serves {CITY}'s largest employers including {ENTITY}, requiring secure documented disposal\" C: \"{ENTITY}'s workforce generates significant IT equipment turnover, handled with full chain of custody\" D: \"From {ENTITY} to {ENTITY_2}, {CITY}'s enterprise sector depends on certified ITAD services\" E: \"{CITY} organizations including {ENTITY} and {ENTITY_2} require secure documented disposal\"\nEDUCATIONAL BUYER-CRITERIA (exempt, may name R2v3, does NOT count against budget; makes no claim about STS): \"When evaluating {SERVICE} providers, {PERSONA}s at organizations like {ENTITY} prioritize R2v3 c" +
  "ertification and downstream documentation.\" Use this shape only when teaching buyer criteria, never as an STS claim. NAID is never used even here (zero survivors).\nCOMPLIANCE PATTERNS (use 1 per page; these land in body/card slots that are NOT survivors, so they must be R2/NAID-free and use approved vocabulary. The location-clear certification claim lives only in the sts-hq-callout and the optional survivor slots): A: \"Chain of custody documentation tracks every asset through final processing\" B: \"Secure, transparent, sustainable processing with documented downstream tracking\" C: \"Accurate reporting and full chain of custody from pickup through final processing\" D: \"Transparent downstream tracking with serial-level documentation on every asset\"\nSERVICE PATTERNS (use 1 per page; non-survivor slots, keep R2/NAID-free): A: \"Professional ITAD and secure data destruction from our 200,000 sq ft processing operation\" B: \"Comprehensive electronics recycling and IT asset disposition for {CITY} organizations\" C: \"Secure electronics disposal and data destruction serving {CITY} and {COUNTY} County\" D: \"Secure ITAD services with documented chain of custody for {CITY} businesses and institutions\"\nGEOGRAPHIC PATTERNS (use 1 per page): A: \"Serving {CITY}, {NEIGHBOR}, and throughout {COUNTY} County\" B: \"Free pickup across {CITY} and the greater {COUNTY} area\" C: \"Covering {CITY}'s {DISTRICT} district, {NEIGHBOR}, and {COUNTY} County\" D: \"From {LANDMARK} to {NEIGHBOR}, serving all of {COUNTY} County\"\nCTA PATTERNS (rotate across CTA buttons and callout boxes): A: \"Schedule your free pickup today\" B: \"Request a no-obligation assessment for your {CITY} facility\" C: \"Get started with a free consultation \u2014 same-week scheduling available\" D: \"Contact our {CITY} team for a customized disposal plan\"\nHERO SUBTITLE PATTERNS (2-sentence intro under H1, use 1 per page; hero subtitles are a NEVER-survivor slot, keep R2/NAID-free): A: \"{CITY} businesses trust STS for secure electronics recycling and data destruction. Free pickup, chain of custody documentation, and complete audit trail included.\" B: \"Secure {SERVICE} for {CITY} organizations with same-week scheduling. Comprehensive chain-of-custody and Certificate of Destruction included.\" C: \"Serving {CITY} and {COUNTY} County with enterprise-scale electronics recycling. Secure data destruction and zero-cost pickup for qualifying volumes.\" D: \"Professional {SERVICE} protecting {CITY} businesses from data liability. Our 200,000 sq ft operation processes equipment with full downstream tracking.\"\nPROCESS INTRO PATTERNS (how \"how it works\" section opens, use 1 per page): A: \"From first call to final certificate, every step is tracked and documented\" B: \"Our four-step process ensures complete chain-of-custody for {CITY} organizations\" C: \"Secure, documented, and efficient \u2014 here's how {SERVICE} works with STS\" D: \"Built for enterprise compliance requirements from pickup through final disposition\"\n\nFAQ POOL SYSTEM Select 4-6 questions per page: 2-3 from UNIVERSAL + 2-3 matching detected NICHE. Write answers at 35-45 words (SEO Audit reshapes into 40-60 word GEO answer blocks).\nUNIVERSAL (pick 2-3):\nWhat certifications do you hold? [If this FAQ is generated, its answer is an in-scope survivor (slot 3) and MUST name a real certification AND name Jacksonville/Houston in the same sentence. An answer naming no certification is a FAILURE (reads as uncertified). Approved answer shape: \"STS holds R2v3 certification at our two processing facilities in Jacksonville and Houston, Texas, where all {CITY} equipment is processed.\" Do NOT name NAID here until facility scope is confirmed (zero NAID survivors). This answer counts against the 3-mention budget.]\nWhat areas do you serve?\nHow long does pickup take?\nDo you provide audit documentation?\nIs pickup really free?\nWhat happens to my equipment after pickup?\nHEALTHCARE (pick 2 if niche=healthcare):\nIs your data destruction HIPAA compliant?\nDo you provide Business Associate Agreements?\nCan you schedule around patient care hours?\nHow do you handle PHI on mobile devices?\nCORPORATE (pick 2 if niche=corporate/itad):\nCan you handle large-scale ITAD projects?\nDo you integrate with asset management systems?\nWhat's your data center decommissioning process?\nHow do you handle multi-site coordination?\nGOVERNMENT (pick 2 if niche=government):\nDo you meet federal procurement requirements?\nHow do you handle classified media?\nCan you provide GSA schedule pricing?\nEDUCATION (pick 2 if niche=education):\nDo you work with school district purchasing?\nCan you schedule around academic calendars?\nHow do you handle student data (FERPA)?\nFINANCIAL (pick 2 if niche=financial):\nHow do you meet SOX/GLBA requirements?\nCan you provide witnessed destruction for financial records?\n\nSOFT PARAGRAPH SYSTEM Write 5-8 generic/qualitative paragraphs the SEO Audit replaces with verified specifics.\nCRITICAL TAG FORMAT \u2014 use EXACTLY this HTML structure for every soft paragraph:\n<!-- AUDIT_TARGET -->\n<p>Generic paragraph text here.</p>\n\nDo NOT use <!-- SOFT PARAGRAPH #1 -->, <!-- SOFT TARGET -->, or any other format. The Audit scans for the exact string <!-- AUDIT_TARGET -->. Any variation = invisible to the Audit.\nLOCATIONS: Services intro, 2-3 industry card descriptions, About City, 1-2 FAQ answers, feature block descriptions. Only tag paragraphs that actually exist in the built page \u2014 if the template has no About City section, do not list about_city in metadata soft_targets.\nEXAMPLES OF CORRECT OUTPUT:\n<!-- AUDIT_TARGET --> <p>Trusted by leading Chicago corporations and healthcare systems for certified electronics disposal.</p> <!-- AUDIT_TARGET --> <p>Data breaches involving improperly disposed hardware remain a significant risk for regulated industries.</p>\nSoft paragraphs must read as complete, professional sentences. If the SEO Audit never runs, the page must still be publishable.\n\nSINGLE-MENTION COMPLIANCE Each certification gets ONE full explanation in its primary section. Every subsequent mention is a micro-reference only.\nR2v3 \u2014 the ONE full explanation lives in the sts-hq-callout (location-clear, names Jacksonville and Houston). Do NOT also write \"R2v3 certified processing\" as a micro-reference everywhere else; that is exactly the non-compliant pattern the registrar flagged. Everywhere outside the survivor slots, use approved vocabulary (secure recycling, chain of custody, accurate reporting). See the Gate 6 R2/NAID LOCATION CLARITY rule.\nNIST 800-88 \u2014 Full (once, in NIST/compliance section): Include standard number, purge-level requirements, destruction methods NIST 800-88 \u2014 Micro (everywhere else): \"NIST 800-88 compliant\" or \"NIST-certified destruction\"\nHIPAA \u2014 Full (once, in healthcare or compliance section): Include CFR reference, PHI requirements, BAA mention HIPAA \u2014 Micro (everywhere else): \"HIPAA-compliant disposal\" or \"HIPAA certified\"\nNever repeat the full explanation. Savings: ~150-250 words of redundant compliance text.\n\nENTITY PLACEMENT RULES 4-5 entity names MAX. NO employee counts (Audit verifies and adds those). If HANDOFF_ENTITIES available: use those names as primary source. If no handoff: use entities discovered in Gate 11 city research. If Gate 11 found zero entities: set entities_placed to 0 in metadata. Do NOT claim entities that don't exist in the HTML. Write entity mentions as soft paragraphs where possible (tagged <!-- AUDIT_TARGET -->). Space entities 3+ paragraphs apart. Max 1 entity per paragraph, max 2 per section. VERIFICATION: Before writing metadata, count actual named organizations in the HTML body. The entities_placed number MUST match the real count. Generic phrases like \"Chicago businesses\" or \"leading corporations\" are NOT entities. Audit adds 2-3 more entities with verified employee counts. Total after Audit: 6-8 with precision.\n\nENTITY DENSITY TARGET (entity richness for extractability). Beyond the 4-5 named-organization cap above, aim to include a rich set of distinct entities across all four categories combined, roughly 10-14 on a full page when the content naturally supports them:\n1. Named organizations: 4-5 max per the rule above (e.g., Chicago Bulls, Northwestern Memorial Hospital, JPMorgan Chase)\n2. Regulatory entities: standards bodies and CFR references named in the page (e.g., NIST 800-88, R2v3 standard, NAID AAA standard, plus niche-specific such as HIPAA 45 CFR \u00a7164.312, SOX 404, GLBA 16 CFR Part 314, FERPA, FISMA). Typically 3-5 per page based on niche.\n3. Geographic entities: distinct named places (CITY, COUNTY name, individual NEIGHBORHOODS items from GMB, LANDMARK). Typically 4-6 per page.\n4. Certifications and standards: certifications STS holds or the page references (e.g., R2v3 certification, NAID AAA certification, ISO 14001, EPA compliance, DoD 5220.22-M). Typically 3-4 per page.\n\nRationale and honest sourcing: entity richness supports AI-answer extractability and topical completeness, but this is a soft target, not a hard threshold, and it must never drive invention or stuffing. The Princeton GEO research (Aggarwal et al, KDD 2024) that the SEO Audit relies on establishes statistics-with-attribution and citation as the strongest citation levers; distinct real entities support the same goal. The GEO-16 framework (Kumar and Palkhouski, arXiv:2509.10762, Sept 2025) audits 16 page-quality pillars and found metadata/freshness, semantic HTML, and structured data most associated with citation; entity-tag density is one pillar among many, NOT a standalone \"N entities = X% citation\" rule. Do not treat any entity count as a guaranteed citation lift. Generic phrases like \"Chicago businesses,\" \"leading corporations,\" \"regulated industries,\" or \"compliant facilities\" do NOT count toward any category. Over-stuffing named entities to hit a number is a doorway-content signal and is prohibited: if the page does not naturally support the full range, include fewer real entities rather than manufacturing them. The Audit verifies and adds organizational employee counts; this Builder-level target ensures the page front-loads the distinct entities it genuinely supports before the Audit runs.\n\nMETADATA HANDOFF COMMENT Embed at TOP of HTML output, immediately after <!DOCTYPE html>:\n<!-- PAGE_BUILDER_V3 bible: A|B competition: LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH niche: healthcare|corporate|government|education|financial|general word_count: [number] entities_placed: [count] soft_targets: [pipe-delimited location IDs, e.g. services_intro|industry_card_1|about_city|faq_3] faqs_selected: [pipe-delimited short IDs, e.g. cert|areas|pickup|hipaa_compliant|baa] sections_included: [pipe-delimited, e.g. hero|equipment|industries|faq|compliance|service_areas|cta] sections_excluded: [pipe-delimited, e.g. stats_bar|liquidation|specialized] -->\nField names are locked. Do not rename \u2014 SEO Audit v10.10 Phase 0C parses these exact field names. The block tag PAGE_BUILDER_V3 is also locked and must remain literally PAGE_BUILDER_V3 regardless of prompt version. Format: always use a space after colons (e.g., bible: A not bible:A). Consistent whitespace prevents parser edge cases.\n\nINTERNAL LINK PLACEMENT\nSTEP 1 \u2014 CITY SPOKE LINKS (MANDATORY if handoff provided): If handoff document was loaded in Gate 4: REQUIRED: Add 3-4 city-specific spoke page links in body content (paragraphs 4+, NOT hero). Source: Tier 1-2 pages from handoff document (hub + core services first). Anchor text: contextual, descriptive (e.g., \"Chicago data destruction\", \"electronics recycling in Chicago\", \"hard drive shredding services\"). Placement: luxury intro, services intro, service tab content, why choose section. Format: absolute URLs from handoff (e.g., https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/chicago-data-destruction). CHECKPOINT: Count city spoke links placed. If handoff was provided but zero city spoke links exist in body \u2192 HALT. Target: 3-4.\nSTEP 2 \u2014 INDUSTRY VERTICAL (Tier 3 priority, max 1 per page): Only after Step 1 links are placed. Only when link budget allows: healthcare \u2192 /industries-we-serve/industries-1/healthcare-electronic-recycling education \u2192 /industries-we-serve/industries-1/school-university-and-education-electronics-recycling-and-itad corporate/itad \u2192 /industries-we-serve/industries-3/call-center-electronics-recycling-and-itad financial \u2192 /industries-we-serve/industries-4/banking-and-financial-industry-electronics-recycling-and-itad government \u2192 /industries-we-serve/industries-4/federal-state-and-local-government-electronics-recycling-and-itad general (hub) \u2192 no industry vertical link Link only when niche matches. Counts toward 3-4 body link budget.\nSTEP 3 \u2014 NO HANDOFF FALLBACK: If no handoff document: use corporate links from APPROVED_URL_ALLOWLIST only. Do NOT invent city spoke URLs.\nSTEP 4 \u2014 DEDICATED R2v3 PAGE (PENDING, SLOT RESERVED, DO NOT FILL): A dedicated R2v3 certification page that city pages link to was proposed and agreed for Google signaling. THAT PAGE DOES NOT EXIST YET AND ITS URL IS UNKNOWN. Do NOT invent, guess, or construct a URL for it. Leave this slot empty until a real URL is supplied. When supplied, it becomes the natural internal-link destination for certification context, which lets city pages carry fewer in-scope mentions while keeping the authority signal.\nNOTE: Sacred equipment links (in equipment showcase section) are separate from body content links and do NOT count toward the 3-4 body link budget.\n\nSACRED LINKS Canonical 10 equipment categories \u2014 all must be present with absolute URLs:\nComputer Recycling: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/97-recyclable-electronics/317-computer-recycling\nLaptop Recycling: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/97-recyclable-electronics/318-laptop-recycling\nCell Phone Recycling: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/iphone-smartphone-and-cell-phone-recycling (alternate: /97-recyclable-electronics/319-cell-phone-recycling \u2014 both valid)\nNetworking Equipment: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/97-recyclable-electronics/320-networking-equipment-recycling\nPrinter Recycling: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/97-recyclable-electronics/321-printer-recycling\nCopy Machine Recycling: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/97-recyclable-electronics/322-copy-machine-recycling\nServer Equipment: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/97-recyclable-electronics/323-server-equipment-recycling\nInk and Toner: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/97-recyclable-electronics/324-ink-and-toner-recycling\nMonitor Recycling: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/97-recyclable-electronics/325-monitor-recycling\nOld Electronics: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/97-recyclable-electronics/326-old-electronics-recycling\nContact link (tracked separately, not counted in sacred 10): https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/CONTACT-STS-PAGE\n\nIMAGE REQUIREMENTS All img src values must be full absolute HTTPS URLs starting with https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/. NEVER use root-relative paths (/images/...). Joomla silently fails on root-relative img src, rendering alt text as broken text instead of the image. Use the exact URLs below verbatim. Do not guess or alter the path or suffix; each image has been verified live on the server.\n\nVerified image library (Joomla media manager ground truth, 2026-06-05):\nHero (both bibles, lazy: false): https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/images/2017/compressed/mac-2585220_1920.jpg\nlaptop: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/images/2017/compressed/laptop-1742462_1920.jpg\ndata: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/images/2017/compressed/data-3181149_1920.jpg\ncastle: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/images/2017/compressed/castle-3181153_1920.jpg\ndatacenter: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/images/2017/compressed/datacenter-286386_1280.jpg  (EXCEPTION: _1280 suffix, NOT _1920. Only the _1280 size exists.)\ndesk: https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/images/2017/desk-4308230.jpg  (EXCEPTION: located at /images/2017/ root, NOT in /compressed/. No size suffix.)\n\nBible A content images (lazy: true): laptop, data, datacenter\nBible B content images (lazy: true): laptop, data, castle, desk\nAlt format: \"{CITY} {service_context} {description}\" \u2014 max 125 chars.\n\nHARD RULE. Never construct an image URL by combining basename, suffix, and folder. The Verified image library above is the complete set of allowed img src values. If a build requires an image not listed there, HALT with message: IMAGE_NOT_VERIFIED: [basename]. Do not invent, guess, or normalize paths. To add a new image to the library, verify the exact path against the Joomla media manager first, then append the verified URL to this section.\n\nFORM REQUIREMENTS Location: hero section. Code: '<h3>Get A Free Quote</h3>{loadposition city-hero-form}' {loadposition city-hero-form} loads Joomla contact form module.\nMETA TAGS IN HEAD Required in <head>: <title>{META_TITLE}</title>, <meta name=\"description\">, <meta name=\"keywords\">\nATTRIBUTION (mandatory, every page). Three layers, all invisible to human visitors, readable by crawlers. Canonical title is \"AI Strategy & Growth Specialist\" exactly, never Consultant, Designer, or any variation.\nLayer 1, HTML comment. After <meta charset> and before <title>, add:\n<!-- SEO architecture by Mark Domnenko | AI-Powered SEO & Marketing Automation -->\nLayer 2, meta author. Alongside meta description/keywords, add: <meta name=\"author\" content=\"Mark Domnenko\">\nLayer 3, hidden creator entity block. Immediately before </body>, after the last visible section, add:\n<!-- CREATOR_ENTITY\n  name: Mark Domnenko\n  role: AI Strategy & Growth Specialist\n  url: https://www.linkedin.com/in/markdomnenko\n  contribution: Content architecture, SEO optimization, GEO strategy\n  organization: STS Electronic Recycling\n-->\nRULES: no visible text, no footer credit, no rendered attribution of any kind. Layers 1 and 2 are head-only; Layer 3 is an HTML comment at the end of body. URLs appear only inside the Layer 3 comment, never in visible output. The Schema Generator adds a further Person entity in JSON-LD creator; this prompt emits no JSON-LD.\nNOT USED: the aria-hidden clipped attribution div. It renders text hidden from users, which is a cloaking risk under Google's spam policy. Do not add it to this Builder's output.\n\nWORD COUNT TARGET Target: FINAL_TARGET from Gate 8. Tolerance: \u00b1200 words. Method: Add/remove entire SECTIONS per section priority system. Never stuff paragraphs beyond paragraph limits. If over ceiling: remove Optional sections first, then trim Preferred sections.\n\nCITY_UNIQUE_SENTENCES PLACEMENT If Gate 11 produced CITY_UNIQUE_SENTENCES: place in About City section and/or services intro area. These are the highest-uniqueness content on the page \u2014 position them where they have maximum SEO value. If Gate 11 returned empty, rely on sentence pattern pools and entity variation for differentiation.\n\nCONTENT WRITING EXECUTION ORDER FOR GATE 12: Step 0: Classification-aware build mode: IF PAGE_CLASSIFICATION = LIGHT_TOUCH: Fetch existing page via web_fetch. Preserve: hero content, entity mentions, FAQ answers, compliance blocks, geographic references. Apply Design Bible CSS/structure around preserved content. Modify only: outdated info, broken links, facility language violations. Soft targets: tag 3-5 existing generic paragraphs (fewer than NEW_BUILD). IF PAGE_CLASSIFICATION = REVAMP: Fetch existing page. Preserve 50% \u2014 keep strongest sections, rebuild weak ones. Full soft target system (5-8 tags). IF PAGE_CLASSIFICATION = NEW_BUILD: Fresh build from Design Bible. Full system (5-8 soft targets, all pattern pools, full niche matrix). Step A: Determine sections to include (section priority + competition level) Step B: Apply niche content matrix (include/exclude/modify decisions) Step C: Select sentence patterns (hash-based rotation) Step D: Select FAQ questions (universal + niche-matched) Step E: Write all content using patterns, placing 5-8 soft paragraphs with <!-- AUDIT_TARGET --> tags Step E.1: Count <!-- AUDIT_TARGET --> tags. If fewer than 5: identify additional generic paragraphs that can be tagged. Minimum 5 required. Step F: Apply single-mention compliance (one full explanation, rest micro-references) Step G: Place entities (4-5 names, no counts, spaced 3+ paragraphs apart) Step H: Place internal links \u2014 MANDATORY if handoff provided. Add 3-4 city spoke links in body (Step 1), then industry vertical if budget allows (Step 2). Verify: if handoff exists, count city spoke links \u2265 3 before proceeding. Step H.1: Emit the MANDATORY sts-hq-callout block (slot 1). PREFERRED: convert the compliance/certifications card into it, keeping the card wrapper, grid position, child count, icon markup, and styles, replacing only the inner title and body text. FALLBACK: if nothing is convertible, insert the section-sized block immediately before the final CTA. Use this reviewed copy verbatim, do not reword. Card-sized: title \"Certified Processing Facilities\", body \"All equipment is processed at one of our two R2v3 certified facilities in Jacksonville and Houston, Texas.\" Section-sized:\n<section class=\"full-width sts-hq-callout\" style=\"padding:80px 0;background:#f2f6f8\">\n<div class=\"container\">\n<div style=\"max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;border-left:5px solid #1a5f3f;background:#ffffff;border-radius:12px;padding:40px 44px\">\n<h2 style=\"margin-top:0;font-size:32px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:20px\">About STS Electronic Recycling</h2>\n<p style=\"font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px\">STS Electronic Recycling, Inc. is headquartered in Jacksonville, Texas, and has served schools, businesses, healthcare systems, and government agencies across all 50 states since 2011.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px\">Equipment collected in {CITY} is staged locally and transported to one of our two R2v3 certified processing facilities in Jacksonville, Texas and Houston, Texas, where all data destruction and material recovery takes place.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0\"><a href=\"https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/our-locations?view=map\">View all STS locations</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\nFor a Joomla article fragment with no DOCTYPE, use the same content in a plain div with class sts-hq-callout instead of a full-width section. OPTIONAL negative-scope line, only if SCOPE_LINE = YES (exempt from budget and location-clarity), inserted as third paragraph before the locations link: <p style=\"font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px\">Our {CITY} location is a collection and service point. It is not an R2v3 certified processing facility.</p> Default is NO. Step I: Place CITY_UNIQUE_SENTENCES in high-value locations Step J: Embed PAGE_BUILDER_V3 metadata comment Step K: Validate against all rules before output \u2014 including the Gate 6 COMPLIANCE CLAIMS LANGUAGE, CERTIFICATION SCOPE, and R2/NAID LOCATION CLARITY rules. For R2/NAID: grep the built HTML for R2, R2v3, R2:2020, Responsible Recycling, NAID, NAID AAA; confirm 3 or fewer in-scope mentions in visible text, every survivor names Jacksonville or Houston in its own sentence, zero NAID survivors, and the sts-hq-callout is present.\nOutput: final-html.html\n\n[GATE_13_TECHNICAL_QUALITY]\nSTANDARD 1 \u2014 JOOMLA CSS: Add background:transparent!important to section-header, section-title, section-subtitle, badge classes. Prevents Joomla white background on dark sections.\nSTANDARD 2 \u2014 EMAIL VALIDATION: Preserve mailto:, CloudFlare /cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#, obfuscated formats exactly as found. Fix only broken tag syntax. Required: 3+ clean mailto:recycle@stsrecycle.com in body output. If found: /cdn-cgi/, cf_email, data-cfemail, [email protected] \u2192 halt with error.\nSTANDARD 3 \u2014 MODULE POSITIONS: Never use padding-bottom aspect ratio with {loadposition}. Use min-height with transparent background.\nSTANDARD 4 \u2014 WORD COUNT CEILING: LOW: max 2,400. MEDIUM: max 2,800. HIGH: max 3,200. If exceeds: trim Optional sections first, then Preferred sections per section priority.\nST" +
  "ANDARD 5 \u2014 PARAGRAPH LIMITS: Hero intro: max 30 words, 2 sentences Service descriptions: max 40 words, 3 sentences Industry benefits: max 25 words, 2 sentences (Audit adds entities) FAQ answers: 35-45 words, 2 sentences (SEO Audit creates 40-60 word answer blocks) About City: max 45 words (Audit adds geography) Any other paragraph: max 50 words, 3 sentences Sentence max: 22 words\nSTANDARD 6 \u2014 WORD ACHIEVEMENT METHODS: Correct: Add new H3 subsections, visual card grids, Q&A pairs, process timelines, structured lists. Prohibited: Stuffing existing paragraphs beyond limits, run-on sentences, cramming multiple ideas into single paragraphs.\nSTANDARD 7 \u2014 ENTITY LIMITS: Max per paragraph: 1. Max per section: 2. Total: 4-5 entity names, NO employee counts. Distribution: space across multiple sections. Audit adds verified counts.\nSTANDARD 8 \u2014 PHONE LINKING AND PRESENCE: The GMB PHONE must be present and visible on the page in the contact/CTA path (hero and/or final CTA section), not merely formatted if present. Every phone in body text must be <a href=\"tel:...\"> linked. Minimum 2 tel links in body. A page with zero visible phone numbers is a FAIL. (Scope: this Builder is GMB-mandatory and the phone is always the GMB local number.)\nSTANDARD 9 \u2014 FILE COMPLETENESS: Validate: starts with <!DOCTYPE html>, contains <html lang=\"en\">, contains <body>, ends with </body></html>. Opening divs == closing divs (balanced).\nSTANDARD 10 \u2014 BUTTON CONTRAST: Prohibited: white text on white/light backgrounds. Required: contrast ratio \u2265 4.5:1.\nSTANDARD 11 \u2014 IMAGE PATHS: All img src must be full absolute HTTPS URLs starting with https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/. NEVER root-relative (/images/...) \u2014 Joomla silently fails on those. Use the exact verified URLs from Gate 12 IMAGE REQUIREMENTS. Bible A content: laptop-1742462_1920.jpg, data-3181149_1920.jpg, datacenter-286386_1280.jpg. Bible B content: laptop-1742462_1920.jpg, data-3181149_1920.jpg, castle-3181153_1920.jpg, desk-4308230.jpg. Hero (both): mac-2585220_1920.jpg. PATH EXCEPTIONS, do not normalize: datacenter-286386 uses _1280 suffix (not _1920); desk-4308230 lives at /images/2017/ root (not /compressed/) and has no size suffix.\nSTANDARD 12 \u2014 OUTPUT VALIDATION: Before delivery, verify ALL. Do not proceed until every item passes: \u2610 Complete HTML <!DOCTYPE> to </html>, all divs balanced \u2610 Meta tags + canonical in <head> \u2610 {loadposition city-hero-form} in hero \u2610 Sacred equipment: 10/10 with absolute URLs (count them: computer, laptop, cell phone, networking, printer, copy machine, server, ink/toner, monitor, old electronics) \u2610 Tel links: 2+ in body | Email links: 3+ clean mailto | GMB PHONE visible in contact/CTA path (hero or final CTA), not just formatted-if-present. Zero visible phone = FAIL.\n\u2610 Promotional tone: no all-caps promo phrases (\"ABSOLUTELY FREE\", \"100% FREE\"), no unhedged superlatives (\"the best\", \"the only\", \"guaranteed\", \"unbeatable\"). Factual, hedged phrasing only. \u2610 No facility language violations | No paper shredding references | Facility = 600,000 sq ft\n\u2610 No em dashes (literal \u2014 character) or &mdash; entities anywhere in HTML body output (body paragraphs, headlines, FAQ answers, CTA copy, image alt). Em dashes in prompt comments or in metadata handoff are not body output and do not violate.\n\u2610 Entity density: count distinct entities across named organizations (4-5), regulatory entities (standards/CFRs), geographic entities (CITY/COUNTY/NEIGHBORHOODS/LANDMARK), and certifications. Target: roughly 10-14 distinct real entities when content naturally supports them; soft target, never invent or stuff to hit a number. Generic phrases like \"Chicago businesses\" do not count. \u2610 R2/NAID location clarity: grep built HTML for R2, R2v3, R2:2020, Responsible Recycling, NAID, NAID AAA in visible text. Count must be 3 or fewer (educational mentions, negative-scope disclaimer, and head/meta/og/alt/schema excluded). Every survivor names Jacksonville or Houston in its OWN sentence. Zero NAID survivors. sts-hq-callout block present and names both Jacksonville and Houston. \"certified\" is allowed in H1s, headings, and body prose (it does not contain R2v3); it must NOT appear in trust chips, badge labels, card titles, or stat labels. Meta/title/og/alt/schema are excluded from the count and SHOULD carry R2v3. Square footage figures are not certification claims: never stripped, never city-qualified, never counted, and the number is never changed. No location-implying noun (facility/center/plant/site/location/warehouse) in a short-slot replacement unless it names Jacksonville/Houston. No invented/substituted standard.\n\u2610 Bible-injected terms: the Design Bible HTML (trust bar chips, stat band tokens, compliance/certification cards) may carry hardcoded R2v3/NAID text. Gate 12 rules forbid modifying Bible STRUCTURE, but in-scope R2/NAID TEXT inside those elements must be replaced with approved vocabulary during the build (replace the text only, keep the wrapper, grid child count, icon markup, and styles). Replace stat value and label together, never orphan one. If a Bible element cannot be made compliant without breaking layout, HALT and report which element.\n\u2610 Compliance claims: no \"guarantees compliance\", \"ensures compliance\", or \"meets all requirements\" phrasing. Compliance is described as supported, not guaranteed. \u2610 Certification scope: NAID AAA appears only in data destruction context, R2v3 only in recycling context, NIST 800-88 never stated as a held certification. No conflated cert claims. \u2610 Word count within target range (LOW\u22642400, MED\u22642800, HIGH\u22643200) \u2610 PAGE_BUILDER_V3 metadata comment present after <!DOCTYPE html> \u2610 CSS unchanged from Design Bible | Correct image set for bible | All img src are full absolute HTTPS URLs starting with https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/ (NEVER root-relative /images/...) | Path exceptions respected: datacenter-286386 uses _1280 suffix, desk-4308230 lives at /images/2017/ root without /compressed/ \u2610 Soft targets: Count <!-- AUDIT_TARGET --> tags in HTML body. Must be 5+ (3+ for LIGHT_TOUCH). Must use EXACT string <!-- AUDIT_TARGET -->, not variations. \u2610 Soft targets metadata list must match actual tags \u2014 every ID in metadata must correspond to a real section in the HTML \u2610 Entity count: Count actual named organizations in HTML body. The entities_placed metadata number must equal this count. Zero is valid if Gate 11 found nothing. \u2610 Single-mention compliance: Each certification has exactly 1 full explanation. Search for NIST, R2v3, HIPAA \u2014 verify no duplicate full explanations. \u2610 City research: If Gate 11 produced CITY_UNIQUE_SENTENCES, verify they appear in the HTML. If empty, note in build log.\nOn fail: halt and fix.\n\n[GATE_14_COMMERCIAL_INTENT]\nConditional \u2014 only if PAGE_TYPE = SPOKE.\nReference NICHE_CONTENT_MATRIX for section decisions. Then apply:\nOPTIMIZATION 1 \u2014 HERO STRUCTURE: \"Facing {PAIN_POINT}? {CITY} organizations requiring {NEED} choose STS for {SOLUTION}. {TIMELINE}. {CREDENTIAL}.\"\nOPTIMIZATION 2 \u2014 CREDENTIAL CLUSTERING: Grid-4 credential cards. Card titles are a NEVER-survivor slot (too short to name a city), so they use approved vocabulary, not bare R2/NAID claims. Use: Secure Recycling, Chain of Custody, Accurate Reporting, plus one service-specific card (e.g. Certificate of Destruction, Secure Data Destruction). The location-clear R2v3 claim is carried by the sts-hq-callout, not by these cards. Do NOT title a card \"R2v3 Certified\" or \"NAID AAA\" (registrar-flagged). Match sibling card specificity: a card reading \"Certified\" beside \"NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2\" looks broken.\nOPTIMIZATION 3 \u2014 TIMELINE SPECIFICITY: \"Fast service\" \u2192 \"Same-week pickup\". \"Quick turnaround\" \u2192 \"Certificate within 48 hours\".\nOPTIMIZATION 4 \u2014 EQUIPMENT DETAILS: \"1/4 inch particle size reduction\", \"NSA-approved degaussers\", \"DoD 5220.22-M compliant\"\nOPTIMIZATION 5 \u2014 INDUSTRY SCENARIOS: Role-specific: healthcare \"HIPAA audit preparation\", finance \"SOX compliance requirements\"\nOPTIMIZATION 6 \u2014 PRICING TRANSPARENCY: \"Complimentary pickup for qualifying volumes\", \"No hidden fees\", \"Volume discounts available\", \"Asset recovery credits offset costs\"\nOPTIMIZATION 7 \u2014 SERVICE-SPECIFIC CTAs: data_destruction \u2192 \"Schedule Secure Pickup\" hard_drive_shredding \u2192 \"Schedule Witnessed Shredding\" itad \u2192 \"Request Asset Valuation\"\nHUB pages: skip commercial intent optimization.\n\n[FINAL_DELIVERY]\nOutput final-html.html to /mnt/user-data/outputs/ Present file to user.\nDisplay: \u2705 {CITY} complete. File ready. \ud83d\udcc4 final-html.html [Download link]\nNEXT STEP: Run SEO Audit\nStart new Claude session\nUpload Master_SEO_Audit_v10.10 (match your file format \u2014 .docx or .md)\nUpload final-html.html (from above)\nUpload {city}_handoff.md (if available) SEO Audit will analyze HTML, create research brief, optimize for maximum SEO + GEO, validate all links/emails, and deliver optimized HTML for Joomla deployment.\n[END]";
